Configuration

You can customize the following variables in the variables.tf file to fit your needs:

    resource_group_name (default: "thrinadh-alerts")
    location (default: "East US")
    app_service_plan_name (default: "thrinadh-app-service-plan")
    function_app_name (default: "thrinadh-function-app")
    application_insights_name (default: "thrinadh-app-insights")
    log_analytics_workspace_name (default: "thrinadh-law")
    alert_email (default: "thrinadh0248@gmail.com")

Example Configuration

Here's an example of how to configure the variables in variables.tf:

hcl

variable "resource_group_name" {
  type    = string
  default = "thrinadh-alerts"
}

variable "location" {
  type    = string
  default = "East US"
}

variable "app_service_plan_name" {
  type    = string
  default = "thrinadh-app-service-plan"
}

variable "function_app_name" {
  type    = string
  default = "thrinadh-function-app"
}

variable "application_insights_name" {
  type    = string
  default = "thrinadh-app-insights"
}

variable "log_analytics_workspace_name" {
  type    = string
  default = "thrinadh-law"
}

variable "alert_email" {
  type    = string
  default = "thrinadh0248@gmail.com"
}

Additional Notes

    Resource Naming: Make sure the names for Azure resources are unique within your subscription.
    Alerts: Alerts are set up for anomalies in Function App failures and HTTP 5xx errors.
    Dependencies: The resources have dependencies to ensure correct provisioning order.

Outputs

The following outputs are defined:

    function_app_name: Name of the Azure Function App
    application_insights_instrumentation_key: Instrumentation Key for Application Insights (sensitive)
    log_analytics_workspace_id: ID of the Log Analytics Workspace
    alert_email: Email address for alerts
